document: docs/adr/0023-the-standard-ships-as-a-plugin-marketplace.md
blob: a1096c5abc6979d993939e0bdb96f615445c3286
decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: How do skills and hooks reach every Claude Code session regardless of how it is opened?

Records the decision to distribute the standard as a Claude Code plugin marketplace declared in the project's .claude/settings.json, keeping engsys claude as a strict reproduction mode.
Translated from Korean to English as a frozen record; the partial reversal of ADR 0007, the quoted ADR 0007 rejection reason and the ADR 0012 pinning argument are preserved.
Headings mapped to Decision / Context and constraints / Rationale and alternatives / Consequences.
The reference to ADR 0007's 「근거와 대안」 section uses that document's current English heading "Rationale and Alternatives", since 0007 is now in English.
Settings keys (extraKnownMarketplaces, enabledPlugins), paths and commands kept verbatim; no Korean literals retained.

